From: ArchR
Subject: [PATCH] fdrv: accept WLAN-only dongles that expose a single interface

With CONFIG_USB_BT the probe insisted on bNumInterfaces == 3 (WLAN plus
the two Bluetooth interfaces) and, when it saw anything else, silently
reclassified an AIC8800DC as an AIC8800DW. The Tenda 2604:0013 rebadge
is WLAN-only: after the u-disk mode switch it enumerates with exactly
one configuration and one vendor-specific interface, iInterface "Wlan"
(read off the device: bNumConfigurations 1, bNumInterfaces 1). So every
probe took the downgrade path and logged "AIC8800DC change to
AIC8800DW".

Accept one interface as well. A single-interface device is a perfectly
valid combo part that simply has no Bluetooth function exposed, and the
interface descriptor check right below still rejects anything that is
not the vendor-specific WLAN interface, so nothing is loosened for
genuinely unsupported layouts.

Same condition used by the aic8800d80 legacy-mcu1 tree, which targets
this chip revision (chip_id=7, chip_mcu_id=1) specifically.

--- a/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
+++ b/aic8800_fdrv/aicwf_usb.c
@@ -2139,7 +2139,7 @@

     /* Check interface number */
 #ifdef CONFIG_USB_BT
-    if (usb->actconfig->desc.bNumInterfaces != 3)
+    if (usb->actconfig->desc.bNumInterfaces != 1 && usb->actconfig->desc.bNumInterfaces != 3)
 #else
     if (usb->actconfig->desc.bNumInterfaces != 1)
 #endif
